From 8452809e45cf39fcaa0e151ad1994edcb47be51b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:11:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] early_shock: vote arms only where vote counts are visible;
 comment arms

Product Hunt hides vote counts for about the first 4 hours: on every clean
day so far (Nov 3, 4, 8, 9, 10) every launch reads 0 votes until hour 4.
The deployed version scored hours 1-3 on those zeros, so its vote arms
there equal the prior and would have been reported as "no gain".

- A cutoff's vote arms count on a day only if >= 50% of its line-up shows
  non-zero votes (detected from the data, not hard-coded).
- New arms: the same shock model on comment counts (public from hour 0),
  with and without popscore inputs; hour 5 added as a cutoff.
- Each arm is scored on the days its signal exists; deltas pair the days
  both arms cover and report how many.
- Readiness is unchanged: hour 5 never decides whether a day is clean
  (still 5 clean days as of Nov 11).
- Status line, outputs and backtests rows keep their format; arms with no
  data are written as n/a and skipped in backtests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
